        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="167.60617368421" YPOS="178.7776" OwnPage="0" ItemID="199663696" PTYPE="6" WIDTH="232.463157894737" HEIGHT="22.7150315789474" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="0" PCOLOR="White" PLINEART="1" PLINEEND="32" path="M0 0 L232.463 0 L232.463 22.715 L0 22.715 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L232.463 0 L232.463 22.715 L0 22.715 L0 0 Z" gXpos="167.60617368421" gYpos="178.7776" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="113.0967" YPOS="141.32010393701" OwnPage="0" ItemID="199666416" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="283.9041" HEIGHT="62.68149606299" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="1" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L283.904 0 L283.904 62.6815 L0 62.6815 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L283.907 0 L283.907 62.6816 L0 62.6816 L0 0 Z" gXpos="113.0967" gYpos="141.32010393701" gWidth="282.55" gHeight="45.4146798798563" ALIGN="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle ALIGN="0" LINESP="28" FONT="Special Elite Regular" FONTSIZE="33" SCALEH="88" KERN="-9"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Confessions of the Fence Eater"/>
                <trail ALIGN="1"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="114.660910526316" YPOS="207.248" OwnPage="0" ItemID="199639088" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="281.243089473684" HEIGHT="356.152" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="2" COLGAP="7.2" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L281.243 0 L281.243 356.152 L0 356.152 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L281.243 0 L281.243 356.152 L0 356.152 L0 0 Z" gXpos="114.660910526316" gYpos="207.247999999987" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" PSTYLE="Default Paragraph Style" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" LINESP="10" FONT="Bell MT Regular" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" LANGUAGE="en_US"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Bold" FONTSIZE="9" CH="Nott N. Annagramm"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Italic" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" CH="Pick-me Pica "/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="     As many of you know, I am about to be expelled from CMU for taking a bite out of the Fence. The vitriol I’ve received from faculty and alumni for this victimless crime has taken a tremendous toll on my mental health, and I would like to present my side of the story."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    It all started when I was holding the Fence for an unnamed organization. I hadn’t eaten in 8 hours, and I couldn’t risk anybody stealing our turf as I snuck off to Ciao Bella. My gaze drifted to the paint-covered picnic table I was sitting at. Beautiful splotches of color pierced the clouds of my dreary mind and empty stomach. Throwing caution to the wind, I scratched a bit off with my fingernail and licked it. It melted in my mouth – bitter yet oh so sweet."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Reader, it was heaven."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    For the rest of that hour, I clawed at that table, chasing that flavor, that feeling. It was bare when I left. Not one person batted an eye at the suddenly drab planks. That gave me confidence. I knew what I needed to do."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    After the club left early that morning, I struck. Armed with a hammer and chisel, I chipped away at one of the Fence’s posts. Once I got a few layers deep, I sunk my teeth in. Oh, how the flavors blended together! The fruitiness of the acrylics, the earthy tones of the warm colors, and the palette-cleansing blacks and whites. Best of all, though, was when I got to nearly the center and I tasted something unique – sweet in a way the other paints hadn’t been, yet oddly familiar. "/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    However, as my tongue worked desperately at that hard-to-reach spot, coaxing sweetness from layer after layer, I heard distant shouts and suddenly felt rough hands tugging at my legs. The CMUPD were brutally forcing me away from my peaceful feast, shouting names to shame my proclivities: “fence-eater,” “maniac,” and “that one weirdo they want to kick out of that club.” "/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Despite the disgusted gazes of my former classmates, I regret nothing. The only person harmed in this fiasco was myself, as I lost two teeth when the officers yanked me off the fence. Yet, as they dragged me to Warner Hall, I finally placed that incredible taste from the Fence’s center:"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    It was exactly like my dorm’s tap water."/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="849.6242" YPOS="1115.1843" OwnPage="-1" ItemID="202240032" PTYPE="2" WIDTH="232.0625" HEIGHT="397.062100000001" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="0.24" LOCALSCY="0.24" LOCALX="-72" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" Pagenumber="0" PFILE="../OneDrive/Documents/GitHub/readme-layout/Vol5/OneDrive/Documents/GitHub/readme-layout/Vol5/5.6 Readme - Scotty Doesn't Know/5.5 images/How to Deal with Those Fuckass Scooters.png" IRENDER="0" EMBEDDED="0" path="M0 0 L232.062 0 L232.062 397.062 L0 397.062 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L232.062 0 L232.062 397.062 L0 397.062 L0 0 Z" gXpos="849.6242" gYpos="1947.1875" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1"/>
