        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="112.3864" YPOS="865.88935384615" OwnPage="1" ItemID="202251200" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="309.116671681416" HEIGHT="91.1371948264162" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="1" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L309.117 0 L309.117 91.1372 L0 91.1372 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L309.117 0 L309.117 91.1367 L0 91.1367 L0 0 Z" gXpos="112.3864" gYpos="865.88615384615" gWidth="282.55" gHeight="45.4146798798563" ALIGN="1" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle ALIGN="1" LINESP="28" FONT="Special Elite Regular" FONTSIZE="33" SCALEH="90" KERN="-10"/>
                <ITEXT SCALEH="90" KERN="-10" CH="What happens if you don't find love during O-week?"/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="113.660910526316" YPOS="636.248" OwnPage="0" ItemID="200599184" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="281.243089473684" HEIGHT="162.879433628318" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="7.2" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L281.243 0 L281.243 162.879 L0 162.879 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L281.243 0 L281.243 162.879 L0 162.879 L0 0 Z" gXpos="113.660910526316" gYpos="636.247999999987" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" PSTYLE="Default Paragraph Style" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" LINESP="10" FONT="Bell MT Regular" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" LANGUAGE="en_US"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Bold" FONTSIZE="9" CH="WP"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Italic" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" CH="Rabitual Brooder "/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="   Rabbit populations follow boom-bust cycles, and the Pittsburgh rabbit sex market is at an all time high. This wreaks havoc on native plants, spreads disease, and takes away from my most enjoyable hobby: being miserable. Sometimes I walk around Westinghouse pond and contemplate drowning myself in two feet of water (I’m 6’5 by the way), and I see a bunny the size of my first nibbling at a clover. Other times, I mope up and down the hills of the Schelney golf course, and see balls of fur hopping into the sunset. How am I supposed to brood under these conditions? The balance of nature is a delicate one, and this is yet another example of how devastating the consequences of upsetting that balance can be.  I can only imagine the suffering of my fellow CMU students; regardless, we must console ourselves with the fact that the rabbits will reach adulthood by midterm season.  "/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="113.0967" YPOS="571.32010393701" OwnPage="0" ItemID="200593520" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="283.9041" HEIGHT="62.68149606299" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="1" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L283.904 0 L283.904 62.6815 L0 62.6815 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L283.907 0 L283.907 62.6816 L0 62.6816 L0 0 Z" gXpos="113.0967" gYpos="571.32010393701" gWidth="282.55" gHeight="45.4146798798563" ALIGN="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle ALIGN="0" LINESP="28" FONT="Special Elite Regular" FONTSIZE="33" SCALEH="84" KERN="-10"/>
                <ITEXT SCALEH="84" KERN="-10" CH="Stupid Baby Rabbits Keep Ruining My Brooding"/>
                <trail ALIGN="1" LINESP="28"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="113.660910526316" YPOS="953.648" OwnPage="1" ItemID="211591936" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="305.71826734979" HEIGHT="349.360849557522" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="7.2" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L305.718 0 L305.718 349.361 L0 349.361 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L305.718 0 L305.718 349.361 L0 349.361 L0 0 Z" gXpos="113.660910526316" gYpos="953.647999999987" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" PSTYLE="Default Paragraph Style" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" LINESP="10" FONT="Bell MT Regular" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" LANGUAGE="en_US"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Bold" FONTSIZE="9" CH="Nott N. Anagram"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Italic" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" CH="Not at all a lobster "/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="   I had just broken up with my girlfriend. She saw someone on the tour of her college she liked more than me. There was an option on the housing form called the “Romance Program.” It said that if you don’t find a partner during O-Week, you will work at an unethical company of your choosing. I chose Palantir. I have a very good memory of faces, so I relate to them a lot."/>
                <para/>
                <tab/>
                <ITEXT CH="There were only options for heterosexual and Welch. Apparently the bisexual program “caused too much drama, and everybody wanted to work for Starbucks.” After a long period of deliberation, I went heterosexual."/>
                <para/>
                <tab/>
                <ITEXT CH="On day 1, I talked to a girl from across the hall. She told me she was majoring in math. I lied that I was too. To impress her, I said that the sum of all integers is -1/12. She slapped me in the face and said a relationship can’t be built on a lie."/>
                <para/>
                <tab/>
                <ITEXT CH="In reality, my major is undecided. In other words, I have no defining characteristics. This makes me fundamentally undateable. My roommate is actually a business major, but he wrote a poem to impress a creative writing major. He showed it to me before he gave it to her. It was the shittiest fucking poem I’ve ever read. The next time I went into my room, they were having sex. I think their defining characteristic is that neither of them are self-aware."/>
                <para/>
                <tab/>
                <ITEXT CH="On day 4, they made us walk over to Schenley Park with tranquilizer guns to hunt for woke students. For each one we caught, we would get one more day to find a partner. I saw one wearing a black shirt with the Fence on it and some words I couldn’t make out, but it ran away before I could shoot it. I didn’t get any extra days."/>
                <para/>
                <tab/>
                <ITEXT CH="On my last day, I got desperate. Math girl from the first day was going to work for OpenAI, so I bought ChatGPT glasses that tell you what to do to make you more attractive to women. I walked up to her and told her I would honestly like to delve into that sweet sweet puss. She shot me with a tranquilizer dart. As my consciousness faded, she said she would make me work for the company nobody wanted to work for and started dragging me to the career center."/>
                <para/>
                <tab/>
                <ITEXT CH="So anyways, that’s how I became the manager of this McDonalds. What was your problem with our refund policy?"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
            </StoryText>
